{
  "sticker": "fishing-boat",
  "called": "the fishing boat",
  "skeleton": "a fishing boat seen from the side, bow to the right: root under the keel; rock (the hull with wheelhouse, mast, crossbar and rigging) on it; swing at the crossbar's left end, where the net's rope hangs from; on swing, the rope (a straight rope piece from the crossbar to the net, drawn behind the crossbar, stretched along its length with sy as it pays out) and the net (the bundle with its floats, on a bone at the knot at the rope's end: lowered by y along the rope as the rope stretches, turned by -swing to keep hanging down). The net never leaves its rope.",
  "sheets": [
    {
      "id": "parts",
      "size": "1536x1024",
      "prompt": "Image 1 is a sticker of a small fishing boat. Draw it as a cut-out paper puppet: its separate pieces laid out on one sheet, the same drawing style, colours, texture, line and proportions as in image 1, every piece at the size it has in image 1 (if they do not all fit, draw them all a little smaller, at the same scale as each other).\n\nDraw each piece on its own, spread out over the sheet with wide empty gaps between them, no piece touching or overlapping another:\n1. the boat WITHOUT its net: the blue-and-white wooden hull, the white wheelhouse with its round windows and funnel, the mast with its crossbar, the bow post, the wooden post at the stern and the rigging ropes, but no net, no orange floats and no rope hanging down to the net.\n2. the net alone as in image 1: the bundled net with its two orange floats and the short rope it hangs by at its top.\n3. the same net swung open: spread out wide and hanging in loose folds, with its two orange floats and the short rope it hangs by at its top.\n\nEvery piece is drawn whole, including what is normally hidden behind another piece, with its edges clean and smooth. It is an object, not a character: no face, no eyes, no mouth. No text, no labels, no numbers, no outline around the pieces beyond the drawing's own line, no shadows, no water, no sand, no splashes or drops. Fully transparent background."
    },
